Title: The Long Way Home
Credit: Written by
Author: Ross Demo Team
Draft date: 2026

INT. KITCHEN - MORNING

SARAH stands at the counter, pouring coffee. Her right arm is wrapped
in a fresh bandage from a kitchen accident yesterday.

SARAH
(wincing)
This is going to slow me down all week.

MIKE enters, checking his watch. It's 1985 — the wall calendar behind
him reads "OCTOBER 1985."

MIKE
We need to leave by eight. The Henderson deal won't close itself.

SARAH
I know. I know. Just let me grab my phone and we'll go.

Sarah picks up a sleek smartphone from the counter and slips it into
her pocket.

INT. CAR - CONTINUOUS

Mike drives. Sarah checks her bandaged right arm in the side mirror.

SARAH
Do you think Henderson noticed I wasn't at the gala last night?

MIKE
He barely noticed you were in the room the year before.

INT. HENDERSON OFFICE - DAY

Sarah shakes Henderson's hand. Her bandage is now on her LEFT arm.

HENDERSON
Sarah. Mike. Good to see you both.

MIKE
We're ready to talk numbers whenever you are.

HENDERSON
Let's not waste the morning. Straight to it.

EXT. HENDERSON OFFICE - DAY

Mike and Sarah step outside, still mid-conversation about the meeting
that just started five minutes ago.

SARAH
That went better than I expected.

MIKE
Two hours well spent. Let's celebrate tonight.

EXT. DOWNTOWN STREET - NIGHT

It is now pitch dark, streetlights glowing, though only minutes have
passed since they left the Henderson meeting at mid-morning.

MIKE
Dinner at eight? I'll book the usual place.

SARAH
Perfect. I'll meet you there.

INT. RESTAURANT - NIGHT

Sarah sits across from Mike. Her bandage has vanished entirely, no
explanation given, no scene of it being removed.

SARAH
To the Henderson deal.

MIKE
To us.

They clink glasses. Sarah discreetly checks a text on her smartphone
under the table.

SARAH
Henderson wants to meet again tomorrow. Says he's impressed.

MIKE
Then tomorrow we close it for good.

FADE OUT.
